"explanation\": \"Pre-vote can precede real term increment; log freshness and voting restrictions qualify grants, current voter aggregation determines election. Higher terms normally force follower, with lease/pre-vote exceptions. Reset discards volatile support and active read tracking; committed log is retained.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-authority\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-authority\",\n        \"S-step\",\n        \"S-reset\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Support is interpreted under applied voter configuration and current leader term. New leader resets remote progress and appends an empty current-term entry before old history can advance through a new current-term commitment. Membership application can reinterpret existing support and directly advance commit. Persistence completion is a separate boundary from protocol receipt.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"B-config\",\n        \"B-authority\",\n        \"B-ready\",\n        \"B-formation\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"S-config\",\n        \"S-reset\",\n        \"S-logcommit\",\n        \"S-send\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Configuration-driven commit and pending-read release asymmetry\",\n      \"Automatic joint exit retry after rejected transfer-time proposal\",\n      \"Pending read messages retained across reset\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [\n      \"Trace startup/restart and snapshot restoration, including membership reconstruction\",\n      \"Trace local async completion constructors and node caller serialization/application ordering\",\n      \"Read changer and heartbeat producer/retry mechanisms supporting the backbone\"\n    ],\n    \"status\": \"incomplete\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Partial source-grounded backbone retained before selecting a focused question; no obligation or defect asserted.\"\n  },\n  \"understanding_changes